iWave Linux extensions

Maintained by Marcin Borecki. This is an independent project, not an official
iWave or NXP firmware distribution. Product and vendor names identify hardware
and source provenance, not sponsorship.

The first profile targets the iWave Telematics Connect Hub G62H with NXP i.MX91,
TCH REL3.3, and the vendor kernel revision
02cf250c2e6bd375c11dae324ea145a39015d41b. It applies the complete ordered vendor
patch set and the documented FlexCAN, BQ25601 and ST LSM6DSx changes.

Original Linux, NXP, iWave, Freescale, STMicroelectronics, Bosch, Pengutronix and
other contributor notices in source files and patches must remain intact. This
repository does not claim ownership of their work. Per-file license terms and
the Linux syscall exception remain applicable.

The public source tree contains no OMAM application, SIM/APN settings, device
credentials, service authority or private deployment profile. Kernel identifiers
such as omam_flexcan are stable interfaces and are preserved for compatibility.

The current public deliverable is a source release. Complete base images remain local. The five retained
external modules still need complete matching-source evidence, and vendor
proprietary libraries/firmware need their applicable redistribution terms. Until
those are resolved, generated firmware archives remain local and are not attached
to public releases. The GPL source project and its native tests can be reviewed
independently of those binary inputs.
